WEBVTT

00:00:05.429 --> 00:00:12.080
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the second of March. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:21.480
<v Grace Liu>We can hear you. I was just saying, my weekend plans were completely scuppered by the weather. Lovely walk turned into two days indoors.</v>

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:28.289
<v Tomasz Nowak>You didn't miss much outside. The football last night, though—honestly, what was that defending?</v>

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:32.859
<v Priya Raman>Not getting into football before I've finished this coffee, thanks.</v>

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:40.219
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Safer subject: the charity bake sale on Friday. That lemon cake was proper good.</v>

00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:47.789
<v Jamie Brennan>At the price you paid, it ought to have been. You went round three times.</v>

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:54.049
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a disciplinary about cake. What's already finished?</v>

00:00:54.359 --> 00:00:58.909
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, so, finished the repair on the line three last night. That's done.</v>

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:04.170
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Not carrying that forward as an open job, then.</v>

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:10.650
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, finished. For once I've got something other than 'waiting for bits'.</v>

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:18.780
<v Jamie Brennan>And I already swapped the filter on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve yesterday. That's another one closed.</v>

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:24.189
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, you clipped out after filter. That was the Boiler Safety Relief Valve?</v>

00:01:24.739 --> 00:01:29.290
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, the Boiler Safety Relief Valve. Yesterday, all done. Not a fresh request.</v>

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Different filter, then: Jamie, can you swap the filter on the compressor one tomorrow?</v>

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.500
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll swap the filter on the compressor one tomorrow.</v>

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:45.439
<v Fiona Doyle>Tomorrow being Tuesday, just so it doesn't get muddled with the one already done.</v>

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.260
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. Yesterday's one finished; compressor one tomorrow.</v>

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:53.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Where are we with production downtime?</v>

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:00.579
<v Grace Liu>First off, the shutdown on the WHB is cancelled now, production need it running.</v>

00:02:02.959 --> 00:02:06.459
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, so that shutdown isn't part of the live plan.</v>

00:02:07.469 --> 00:02:10.620
<v Grace Liu>No. Cancelled, not just pushed back a few hours.</v>

00:02:11.349 --> 00:02:19.050
<v Grace Liu>Separate to that, I'll schedule downtime for the Injection Moulding Line 2 with production tomorrow morning. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:26.379
<v Fiona Doyle>That's getting the downtime scheduled tomorrow morning, rather than saying the line's definitely stopping tomorrow morning?</v>

00:02:28.729 --> 00:02:34.680
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, exactly. I'll do the scheduling with production tomorrow morning. We haven't agreed the actual stop yet.</v>

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace Liu. Yours for tomorrow morning, and understood on the urgency.</v>

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.750
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, talking over you—so that isn't tied to the cancelled WHB shutdown?</v>

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:51.860
<v Grace Liu>No, separate thing entirely. The WHB shutdown stays cancelled.</v>

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:58.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace, can you grease and check the bearings on the AC1 tomorrow, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:03:00.949 --> 00:03:06.550
<v Grace Liu>Yep, I'll grease and check the bearings on the AC1 tomorrow, whenever I get a chance.</v>

00:03:07.509 --> 00:03:12.409
<v Tomasz Nowak>Just the grease and bearing check, yeah? Not a strip-down hiding in the wording?</v>

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:18.120
<v Grace Liu>Just grease and check the bearings. That's what I'm taking.</v>

00:03:20.449 --> 00:03:23.250
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right. Nothing bigger being slipped in there.</v>

00:03:23.729 --> 00:03:33.180
<v Jamie Brennan>While we're on things people might read too much into, noticed the line 1 mould temp was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:03:35.009 --> 00:03:37.810
<v Priya Raman>Settled down again, rather than still sitting high?</v>

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:45.270
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, settled. Just passing on what I saw, not asking for a job on it.</v>

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.479
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Observation only.</v>

00:03:47.889 --> 00:03:54.189
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same sort of update from me: heard a slight rattle from the 11kV board, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:59.699
<v Priya Raman>Right, you're flagging an observation, not handing over an intervention on the board.</v>

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:04.639
<v Tomasz Nowak>Exactly. Nothing to action yet, that's all I'm saying.</v>

00:04:05.919 --> 00:04:08.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. And the bits you're waiting on?</v>

00:04:09.639 --> 00:04:14.889
<v Tomasz Nowak>The supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the line one. So that's still blocked.</v>

00:04:16.129 --> 00:04:23.480
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, there's no confirmed delivery date to build anything round. Same blocker, not a new purchasing action out of this meeting.</v>

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:30.110
<v Tomasz Nowak>And still waiting on parts for the palletiser, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.879
<v Fiona Doyle>Both staying blocked, then. Neither is being promised as work for today.</v>

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:42.300
<v Tomasz Nowak>Correct. See, I knew I'd get back to 'waiting for bits' eventually.</v>

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:51.850
<v Sarah Okafor>PR, can you do a site visit at the warehouse with the contractor this morning? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:53.410 --> 00:05:00.759
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll do a site visit at the warehouse with the contractor this morning. Understood, important but not an urgent dash.</v>

00:05:02.779 --> 00:05:07.329
<v Fiona Doyle>And we're talking about the visit itself, not agreeing any contractor works here?</v>

00:05:09.519 --> 00:05:15.470
<v Priya Raman>Just the site visit at the warehouse with the contractor, this morning. Nothing beyond that being agreed.</v>

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:18.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Spot on, thanks.</v>

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:28.779
<v Jamie Brennan>Um, I'll send the shift handover report round as well. That's fairly important, with all these finished and blocked bits getting mixed together.</v>

00:05:31.209 --> 00:05:36.459
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I've heard 'filter' twice and nearly made it the same job in my head.</v>

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:43.970
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. I'll send the shift handover report round; I'm not volunteering another repair along with it.</v>

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:49.079
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Jamie Brennan. You've got the report, fairly important.</v>

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:53.019
<v Fiona Doyle>Quick check I've followed: Jamie, compressor one filter tomorrow.</v>

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.290
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, that's mine for tomorrow.</v>

00:05:56.459 --> 00:06:04.160
<v Fiona Doyle>Grace, scheduling with production for the Injection Moulding Line 2 tomorrow morning, not urgent; AC1 bearings tomorrow whenever you get a chance.</v>

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:12.930
<v Grace Liu>That's it. I'll schedule the downtime tomorrow morning, and grease and check the bearings on the AC1 tomorrow. Both as we've said.</v>

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:19.060
<v Priya Raman>And I've got the warehouse visit with the contractor this morning. All clear my end.</v>

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:27.040
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Finished work stays finished, cancelled shutdown stays cancelled, and those parts blockers are still blockers. No mystery extra jobs.</v>

00:06:29.189 --> 00:06:32.689
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No mystery extra cake either. Friday's lot has definitely gone.</v>

00:06:34.319 --> 00:06:37.120
<v Tomasz Nowak>Mostly into you, by the sound of it.</v>

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:43.730
<v Grace Liu>At least somebody enjoyed their weekend. I've still got wet walking boots by the radiator.</v>

00:06:45.079 --> 00:06:48.230
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, on that glamorous note, thanks everyone. That's us.</v>
